WEBVTT

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:13.860
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:14.070
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.030
<b>Everything Becomes F: The Perfect Insider</b>

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:43.040
<b>Chapter Six                      Crimson Resolve</b>

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:55.550
Saikawa-sensei! Wait, please!

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:58.420
I apologize for trying to hit you!

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:01.890
That isn't it.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.220
Let's go back.

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:04.700
Everyone's waiting.

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.150
Are we really leaving the island?

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.600
That's always been the plan.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.940
What about the case?

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:13.230
We haven't solved a single thing yet.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:16.800
I know it has to be eating away at you!

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.240
The police will be here later.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.500
The murderer may still be in the lab.

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:31.670
You understand what I'm trying to tell you, right?

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.590
Um, but...

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.840
Then let me ask this.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:39.810
Do you have a good reason for wanting to stay?

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.180
Something that can persuade me?

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.260
Well...

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:46.520
No. So let's go back.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.070
Sensei!

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.450
Where have you been?!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:03.450
If you'd thought logically, you'd have known 
the lab was the sole possibility.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.010
Where's everyone else?

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.420
Playing at the beach.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.030
I... I was so worried

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.020
about you two, I stayed here!

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.320
There was a bit of trouble...

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.090
Yeah, after what happened, I'm tired.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.180
After what happened?

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:23.530
I'm going to take a nap.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:26.130
Me, too.

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.360
W-W-Wait!

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.600
What happened?

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.610
Let's begin the meeting.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.290
I'll go over everything

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:41.110
that happened in the lab last night.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.520
I want your honest opinions.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.300
She came out.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.840
So you told him you liked him?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.790
Well, if you ask me,

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.270
a full evening is too long.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:09.170
When you want to confess your feelings, 
you should be more direct.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.000
It seems she got rejected.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:14.930
Alcohol.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.130
At times like these,

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:20.320
I think you need to drink!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.160
You're a minor.

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.730
Two people are dead.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.410
But I can't say anything more...

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:28.760
Someone bring some alcohol.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.060
If we get her something non-alcoholic—

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:38.850
So this is...

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:39.700
Non-alcoholic.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:41.010
And? And?

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.750
Two people are dead.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:47.140
One was killed in a locked room.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:50.830
The other, by contrast, was killed outdoors.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.160
What they have in common is

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.350
that they belong to the Magata family.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.040
Dr. Shiki Magata and Director Shindo.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.860
This means the daughter and younger brother

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:06.950
of Magata Sachiro, who died fifteen 
years ago, were both killed.

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:11.480
When we consider who the killer could be,

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.140
we must first consider who stands to gain from this.

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:17.840
Magata Shiki's room was

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:20.410
as perfectly sealed as you can get.

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:24.940
No one should have been able to enter or leave.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:28.310
But she was killed.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:31.250
Which means the killer was in the room.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.490
But the security cameras

00:05:33.490 --> 00:05:36.440
didn't show anyone entering the room.

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:39.460
When did they enter and how?

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.630
And how did they get out?

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:48.460
That aluminum door can be opened 
from the doctor's side,

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:50.710
but only she could do it.

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.820
To open the door, her right hand is required.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.240
But even if we assume that's why it was amputated,

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.740
that gives us no answer as to 
why her legs were cut off.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:06.550
Simple camouflage?

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:10.230
Or is there some reason, after all?

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.240
That room was sealed for fifteen years.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.490
The living space was carefully cleaned.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.910
No one went in. No one left.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.560
And no one was inside.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.070
A robot which locks and unlocks doors.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.960
Blocks.

00:06:27.670 --> 00:06:29.280
Deflated balloons.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:31.410
A stuffed bear.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:33.590
A sewing machine and patchwork.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:38.440
The strange messages left on the computer 
from three different people.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:39.840
Three people?

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.100
Does that mean that someone other than 
Dr. Magata Shiki was in the room?

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.430
No, she was the only one.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:50.220
The other two lived inside her head.

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.590
Multiple personalities, right?

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:53.550
Yes.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.580
It seems she'd recreated the people around her

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:00.690
who'd died, as new personalities.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:04.820
<b>— Magata Shiki</b>

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.820
The first was her twin brother, 
who died shortly after birth,

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:10.280
<b>— Kurimoto Kishio</b>

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:06.270
Kishio-san.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:10.950
The second was Suma-san, the maid who 
took care of her when she was young.

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:15.660
<b>— Sasaki Suma</b>

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.660
And a doll that was thrown away 
after it was covered in blood,

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.410
<b>Michiru</b>

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:16.950
Michiru.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.480
Do you mean that she left messages

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:24.460
from each of her different personalities?

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.800
Saikawa-sensei believes not.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:32.770
If nothing else, Dr. Magata 
didn't write the messages.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:34.810
If she had,

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:38.330
it would mean she'd foreseen her death.

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:41.250
And it's unbelievable that 
three different personalities

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.530
could each write messages in such a short time.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.510
Everything is too perfect.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:49.230
Which means they must

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.790
have been written by the killer.

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.470
And those words, as well.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.330
Those words whose meaning I don't know.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:06.490
The biggest mystery of this case.

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.170
"Everything...

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.170
...becomes F."

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.920
<b>Everything Becomes F</b>

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:15.170
Anyway, so we basically know nothing!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:20.310
Why did the system go out of control?

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.970
And does the fact that Dr. Magata's sister, Miki-san,

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:26.560
came to the lab at this time mean something?

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:31.280
What was the purpose of that robot, Michiru?

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:35.830
And what is the significance of Magata 
Sachiro's statement before his death,

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.210
"I won't let you do this"?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.320
When we answer all these questions,

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.290
we'll know who it was

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:48.910
that killed Dr. Magata and Director Shindo.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.880
And so, this is what I think!

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:58.640
This has something to do with what 
happened fifteen years ago.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:02.840
Dr. Shiki was overcome by death.

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:04.810
Overcome by death?

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.440
She tried to make me remember 
my parents' deaths.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.360
You lost your parents, did you not?

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:14.790
Do you remember that day?

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.200
She wanted to know

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:20.570
how I felt when my parents died.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.190
But Sensei...

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.290
Sensei?

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:28.140
She must mean Saikawa-sensei.

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.380
He's trying to run away from all the mysteries.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.670
Saikawa-sensei...

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.890
It's hot out here, isn't it?

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:41.700
Any developments?

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:50.240
Actually, we have a request for you.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:55.790
We're well aware of how selfish it is.

00:09:55.790 --> 00:09:56.900
Wait.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:59.060
This isn't one of those requests

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.910
that I can't turn down once I hear it, right?

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.100
We decided it at the meeting.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.400
It's not my personal desire.

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.420
Even without your agreement—

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:13.420
You want to hide the fact that Dr. Magata is dead?

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.220
I refuse.

00:10:20.210 --> 00:10:21.600
You see,

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.310
the lab has the contract for a major 
project coming up next week.

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:29.510
It's for NASA.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:33.260
We've been working on it for a year.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.900
I understand your situation, 
but I can't agree to that.

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:38.090
Just for a week...

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:42.200
If her body's found next week...

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:45.330
I won't say that it will all work out,

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.220
but we can get through somehow.

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.330
And what about Director Shindo?

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:54.460
We'll leave that to the police.

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:57.090
Someone killed him.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.560
We'll have them investigate that.

00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.340
Once that investigation starts,

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:04.520
how do you intend to hide the 
fact that Dr. Magata isn't here?

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.570
We have her sister, Miki-san.

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.230
That won't work!

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:13.680
Lately, Dr. Magata has appeared 
in the media in small amounts.

00:11:14.570 --> 00:11:17.450
If you try to use her as a double, 
they'll realize immediately.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:19.760
I know that, of course.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.530
She'll just take over the director's position.

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.490
She's already agreed.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.150
Right now, I just want

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:31.500
to focus on getting through the next week.

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:35.790
Yamane-san,

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:39.570
would you please not make my 
impression of you any worse?

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.850
The cutting-edge design of that lab...

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.490
The lifestyle you all lead there...

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:54.240
If I'd known about it in high school,

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.840
I'm sure I would have

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.320
decided to spend my life within it.

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:03.660
Yes, I agree.

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:05.720
Please go.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.820
I'm leaving the island on the ship tomorrow.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.850
We're packing up the leftovers.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.900
You want some?

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:44.250
No, thanks. My stomach isn't feeling well.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.700
Where's Nishinosono-kun?

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.170
Asleep in her tent.

00:12:51.550 --> 00:12:53.580
It was a rough time...

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.250
Half of those are hers.

00:12:56.510 --> 00:12:58.130
She was pretty upset.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:00.190
She's a minor, though.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:01.760
They're non-alcoholic.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:03.090
But...

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:06.280
She's a mean drunk.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.750
That's strange...

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.320
When did it get to be night?

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:19.740
How do you feel?

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.140
Still a little light-headed.

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:25.280
They told me you drank non-alcoholic beer.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:26.530
I know that!

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.540
It's just a lot of bad things have happened.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.040
Bad things?

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.830
Two people were killed.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.440
I got in a fight with you.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:42.550
And the fact that you insist on going home.

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.060
But it's okay...

00:13:46.060 --> 00:13:48.320
I'm light-headed now, so it's okay.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:49.800
That...

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:52.670
There was one lying on the ground.

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:54.060
Want to do it?

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:56.470
Sure.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:08.360
When I was a kid, I was scared of fireworks.

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.190
I couldn't hold one of these.

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:13.870
A sparkler?

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:18.070
I wondered why everyone was so happy, 
doing something so dangerous.

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:25.990
Sensei...

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.510
I'm staying on the island, too.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.560
I didn't say I was staying.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:39.320
You didn't say it aloud, but you said it.

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:40.820
Those fireworks...

00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:45.430
You understand how people feel

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:47.780
when they willingly do 
something dangerous, right?

00:14:48.150 --> 00:14:52.510
Even if it's dangerous, you want to return 
to the lab and solve the mystery.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:53.850
No, I—

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.540
I feel the same.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:58.580
I figured out why I want to stay.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:00.510
I want to know

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.250
what she wanted to tell me.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.620
Why she agreed to meet me.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:11.300
Why she asked about my parents' accident.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.380
There must be some meaning there.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:15.760
Meaning?

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:17.370
I don't know,

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:20.010
but something that will help solve this case.

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.000
And I also...

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:23.330
You also?

00:15:23.630 --> 00:15:26.910
Anyway, I don't think I can run away!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:29.610
If I look away from what I'm facing now,

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.160
I'll regret it the rest of my life!

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:34.620
But that kind of directness

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.450
can destroy the things you care about.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.590
Some things are better looked away from—

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:42.290
I don't care, as long as you're here.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:51.810
In the end, you're relying on me.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:53.110
Is that a problem?

00:15:57.430 --> 00:15:59.890
You're going back to the lab right now?!

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.490
We may not be back for a while.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:03.760
Take care of everyone.

00:16:03.760 --> 00:16:04.390
But—

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:04.980
Understood.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.310
Goodbye.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:07.320
Kunie-sensei!

00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.290
Tomorrow afternoon, the boat 
will come to pick you up.

00:16:10.690 --> 00:16:12.980
Right. You take care.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:15.950
What do you mean?

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:20.100
Can you give us permission 
to investigate the facility?

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:24.420
Saikawa-sensei and I will find the 
killer before the cops arrive.

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:25.710
In exchange,

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.680
we'll help you with the cover-up for one week.

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:34.180
Bravo.

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:39.580
Can you print out a list of everything 
Dr. Magata had sent to her room?

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:40.300
Yes.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.180
For what time period?

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:44.190
The last year or so?

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:45.130
Roger.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:51.450
And I want to see the footage 
of when it happened again.

00:16:51.450 --> 00:16:52.410
Sure thing.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.680
In slow motion.

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:27.940
Huh?

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.230
Play that once more.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.510
Wait... Stop it.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:38.350
Look here.

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:40.780
The elevator is displaying "B2."

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:43.700
I can't see. It's too small.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.110
I can't either, but it's two characters, right?

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:49.380
The other two are "R" and "1." 
Both are one character.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:51.060
This has to be B2!

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.730
So what does that mean?

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:55.590
Go forward.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:17:58.800
Stop.

00:17:59.290 --> 00:18:00.640
Look carefully!

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:02.720
The elevator's number is changing.

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:06.100
It isn't on B2! It's on R!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.740
When the body came out, the elevator was on B2,

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.370
and then it moved to the roof.

00:18:11.370 --> 00:18:12.630
That's right...

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:15.530
Someone summoned it from the roof!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.640
So they moved by elevator?

00:18:23.850 --> 00:18:25.290
Let's hurry.

00:18:33.530 --> 00:18:35.800
I'll look in the bedroom.

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:02.320
Hey, Michiru?

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.690
Yes, I am Michiru.

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.330
Are you alone?

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:08.030
To be alone is lonely.

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:09.580
Lonely is seven.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:12.090
It's saying the same thing as Dr. Magata.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:10.960
Seven is a number.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:13.790
Very philosophical.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:16.450
Did you know what she meant?

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.510
There's something interesting. Come with me.

00:19:24.020 --> 00:19:25.680
What about them?

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.110
All of them only reach volume 15.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:31.520
<b>Insects of the World 

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:32.710
You're right!

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.070
So there you go.

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:35.650
What do you mean?

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.330
Fifteen.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:39.150
Fifteen?

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:40.360
Fifteen years.

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:43.490
Dr. Magata was here for fifteen years.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.990
Everything is fifteen...

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.080
"Fifteen."

00:20:20.230 --> 00:20:21.210
I'll do it.

00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:21.890
Shiki!

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:52.750
I won't

00:20:53.890 --> 00:20:56.400
let you do this!

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:20.430
Good evening, Aunt Yumiko.

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:25.030
But it looks like you're a little late.
